naturally|without-artificial-help|ADVERB|through natural processes|In a way that happens through nature rather than through artificial methods.|một cách tự nhiên|The pond fills naturally when rainwater flows down the hillside.|Ao đầy nước một cách tự nhiên khi nước mưa chảy xuống sườn đồi.|Often modifies a process: grow naturally, occur naturally. Not all natural processes are harmless.|0
naturally|as-expected|ADVERB|as one would expect|Used to show that something is understandable or expected.|đương nhiên; như có thể dự đoán|Naturally, the children were curious about the unopened parcel.|Đương nhiên, bọn trẻ tò mò về gói bưu kiện chưa được mở.|Sentence adverb, often separated by a comma. It comments on the statement rather than describing a physical process.|1
stair|single-step|NOUN|step in a staircase|One of the steps used to move between levels in a building.|bậc cầu thang|A loose stair creaked whenever someone climbed to the attic.|Một bậc cầu thang bị lỏng kêu cót két mỗi khi có người lên gác mái.|Countable for one step; stairs usually refers to the whole set: go up the stairs.|0
yawn|open-mouth-tired|VERB|make a tired mouth movement|To open your mouth widely and take a deep breath, often when tired.|ngáp|Nam yawned halfway through the late film and decided to go to bed.|Nam ngáp giữa chừng khi xem bộ phim chiếu muộn rồi quyết định đi ngủ.|Intransitive; yawned, yawning. A yawn does not always mean boredom.|-
dentist|tooth-care-professional|NOUN|professional who treats teeth|A trained professional who examines and treats teeth and gums.|nha sĩ|The dentist explained how to clean around the new filling.|Nha sĩ giải thích cách vệ sinh quanh chỗ trám mới.|Countable; see a dentist, make an appointment with a dentist. The dentist's can mean the surgery.|0
faint|lose-consciousness-briefly|VERB|briefly lose consciousness|To become unconscious for a short time.|ngất xỉu|During the rehearsal, an actor fainted and the performance stopped.|Trong buổi diễn tập, một diễn viên ngất xỉu và buổi diễn dừng lại.|Intransitive verb; fainted. This is not the adjective meaning weak or difficult to notice.|-
